{
  "manufacturer": "Seneca",
  "manufacturer_slug": "seneca",
  "model": "R-32DIDO Ethernet I/O (32 digital inputs/outputs)",
  "model_slug": "r-32dido",
  "short_model": "R-32DIDO",
  "aliases": [
    "R32DIDO",
    "R-32DIDO-1",
    "R-32DIDO-2",
    "Seneca R series 32DIDO"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (remote I/O module, digital inputs/outputs)",
  "applies_to": "R-32DIDO (R-32DIDO-1 / R-32DIDO-2) in the Series R I/O manual MI-00604-29-EN.",
  "summary": "The R-32DIDO is a Seneca R-series remote I/O with 32 digital channels that can each be set as input or output, each with a 32-bit counter. It serves Modbus TCP on Ethernet and Modbus RTU on RS-485. This map covers the two 16-bit I/O words, the 32 counters and the coil and discrete-input views of each channel.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP",
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 38400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Holding-register tables print the 4x number (40001) and the 0-based offset (0); coils print 1 / offset 0 and discrete inputs 10001 / offset 0. The offset is the wire address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Series R I/O with protocol - User Manual",
    "doc_number": "MI-00604-29-EN",
    "revision_date": "2026-09-03",
    "url": "https://www.seneca.it/media/6848135/mi00604-29-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Modbus conventions pp. 95-100; R-32DIDO tables pp. 101-130; defaults in the web-server chapter pp. 31-35"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The protocol page lists function codes 01, 03, 05, 06, 15 and 16; the tables also give the digital inputs as 1x input status read with function 02. Modbus RTU runs on RS-485 and Modbus TCP serves up to 8 clients.",
    "Counters are printed MSW at the lower address (counter 1 MSW 40101, LSW 40102), so they are ABCD.",
    "Factory settings from the manual: static IP 192.168.90.101/24, gateway 192.168.90.1, Modbus TCP port 502, station address 1; RS-485 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, address 1.",
    "Left out: period and frequency floats (40165-40292), because their rows do not mark which word is MSW and a sibling product in the same manual uses LSW first; the command and status registers, whose codes are not listed for this product; the large configuration and P2P rule block from 45001.",
    "The discrete-input table prints its rows as RW; discrete inputs are read-only by protocol and are listed as R."
  ],
